DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The lliibbuuggiiddffww library routines provide an interface to the
     mac_bsdextended(4) file system firewall MAC policy.

     The lliibbuuggiiddffww library defines the following functions:

     bbssddee__rruullee__ttoo__ssttrriinngg()     Converts the internal representation of a rule
                               (_s_t_r_u_c_t _m_a_c___b_s_d_e_x_t_e_n_d_e_d___r_u_l_e) into its text
                               representation; see bsde_rule_to_string(3).

     bbssddee__ppaarrssee__rruullee()         Parses an entire rule (in argument array form);
                               see bsde_parse_rule(3).

     bbssddee__ppaarrssee__rruullee__ssttrriinngg()  Parses an entire rule string; see
                               bsde_parse_rule_string(3).

     bbssddee__ggeett__rruullee__ccoouunntt()     Returns the total number of ugidfw rules being
                               enforced in the system; see
                               bsde_get_rule_count(3).

     bbssddee__ggeett__rruullee__sslloottss()     Returns the total number of used rule slots;
                               see bsde_get_rule_slots(3).

     bbssddee__ggeett__rruullee()           Returns a rule by its rule number; see
                               bsde_get_rule(3).

     bbssddee__ddeelleettee__rruullee()        Deletes a rule by its rule number; see
                               bsde_delete_rule(3).

     bbssddee__sseett__rruullee()           Uploads the rule to the mac_bsdextended(4) mod‐
                               ule and applies it; see bsde_set_rule(3).

     bbssddee__aadddd__rruullee()           Upload the rule to the module, automatically
                               selecting the next available rule number; see
                               bsde_add_rule(3).

